{audience_instruction}
Give {member_full_name} a precise, varied dispatch receipt. When the recipient DM is delivered, wording such as The delivery to RECIPIENT was successful is welcome; use the supplied mention for RECIPIENT. If a public post was requested, state its separate recorded status.
Recipient: {recipient_full_name}; validated mention: {recipient_mention}. Overall status: {delivery_status}; recipient DM: {dm_status}; public post: {public_status}; once-only XP result: {xp_result}. Authoritative summary: {summary}. If details are not recorded, omit them and use the summary. Only delivered is success; queued/pending is not yet confirmed, partial is not complete, and failed/cancelled is not successful. Do not imply the recipient read the message, promise retries or award XP again.

